{"name":"Northern Hemisphere","hex":"#017466","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Northern Hemisphere","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The hemisphere in Earth to the north of the Equator, in which 90% of the total land area on Earth is located."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Northern_Hemisphere"}],"entries":[{"title":"Northern Hemisphere","blocks":[{"text":"The Northern Hemisphere is the half of Earth that is north of the equator. For other planets in the Solar System, north is defined as being in the same celestial hemisphere relative to the invariable plane of the Solar System as Earth's North Pole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Northern_Hemisphere_LamAz.png/330px-Northern_Hemisphere_LamAz.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Hemisphere","wikidata":"Q39061"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Hemisferio_Norte.png/500px-Hemisferio_Norte.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Hemisferio_Norte.png/500px-Hemisferio_Norte.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Northern Hemisphere is highlighted in yellow. The hemispheres appear to be unequal in this image because Antarctica is not shown.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHemisferio_Norte.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Northern_icesheet_hg.png/500px-Northern_icesheet_hg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Northern_icesheet_hg.png/1280px-Northern_icesheet_hg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Nor